SUMMARY:ACES Horizon Talk: Book Talk with Dr. Eveline Washul
DESCRIPTION:Dr. Eveline Washul will discuss her new book\, High Lands\, P
 ure Earth: Place Making\, History\, and Urban Transitions on the Tibetan 
 Plateau (Cornell 2026). In the twenty-first century\, China's accelerated
  urbanization has transformed the Tibetan Plateau. Yet Tibetan urban expe
 riences continue to be profoundly shaped by senses of being in the world 
 that long predate Tibet's subjugation into the modern Chinese nation-stat
 e. Combining novel analysis of Tibetan textual sources\, ethnographic res
 earch\, and Indigenous studies frameworks\, Washul's book explores how Ti
 betans actively engage history\, peoplehood\, and place to build belongin
 g and community even in urban spaces characterized by intense state-led d
 evelopment and assimilation.Please note that this event will be in person
  only. There will not be a Zoom or hybrid option. Lunch will be provided.
 This event is sponsored by:Department of Central Eurasian StudiesInner As
 ian and Uralic National Resource CenterDepartment of AnthropologyEast Asi
 an Studies CenterDepartment of East Asian Languages and CulturesNative Am
 erican and Indigenous Studies Program
