  book\, <i>High Lands\, Pure Earth: Place Making\, History\, and Urban Tr
 ansitions on the Tibetan Plateau</i> (Cornell 2026). In the twenty-first 
 century\, China's accelerated urbanization has transformed the Tibetan Pl
 ateau. Yet Tibetan urban experiences continue to be profoundly shaped by 
 senses of being in the world that long predate Tibet's subjugation into t
 he modern Chinese nation-state. Combining novel analysis of Tibetan textu
 al sources\, ethnographic research\, and Indigenous studies frameworks\, 
 Washul's book explores how Tibetans actively engage history\, peoplehood\
 , and place to build belonging and community even in urban spaces charact
 erized by intense state-led development and assimilation.</p><p><strong>P
 lease note that this event will be in person only</strong><strong>. There
  will not be a Zoom or hybrid option. Lunch will be provided.</strong></p
