SUMMARY:Hamilton Lugar School Study Abroad Photo Competition
DESCRIPTION:$100 first-place prize in each category          Top 3 photos
  in each category will be displayed in GISB Atrium\, Nov 16 - 20.        
   Winning photos will be permanently displayed in the Global and Internat
 ional Studies Building.    Who can enter?  Any HLS student who studied ab
 road Fall 2025\, Spring 2026\, Summer 2026 or Academic Year 2025-2026.  P
 hotos must have been taken during your study abroad experience in your ho
 st country.Photo Submission CategoriesMost Picturesque: Capture a memorab
 le landscape\, cityscape\, landmark\, or other scene from your host count
 ry    Cultural Exchange: Share a moment that reflects meaningful engageme
 nt with or learning about your host community and culture    A Day in the
  Life:&#160\;Show us a moment that captures what everyday life was like d
 uring your time abroad.    Photos that feature you and your IU spirit are
  encouraged!A few things to know before you submit:  Photos should tell t
 he story of your study abroad experience while respectfully representing 
 the people and places you encounteredMake sure people pictured are comfor
 table being photographed and having the photo publicly displayed  Photo f
 eaturing children or minors are not permitted  Do not submit photos featu
 ring dangerous/prohibited activities\, alcohol or drugs.&#160\;  Avoid ph
 otos that stereotype\, exploit\, or disrespect people or cultures  Follow
  photography rules at religious\, memorial\, governmental\, and culturall
 y significant sites  Review the full photo ethics and contest guidelines 
 (https://indiana-my.sharepoint.com/:w:/g/personal/ellcohen_iu_edu/IQCuZXL
 _BuC3SJQbjsVO7gvaAbUpX29xqtIFzjJ7JXaPBlY?e=6PUNCr)Photo Specifications  S
 ubmit your original\, highest resolution photo (preferably 900 x 720 mega
 pixels or greater)–not a screenshot or imagine downloaded from social m
 edia.  Low-resolution images may be removed from consideration.  Accepted
  file types: JPEG\, PNGSubmit your photos here (https://forms.cloud.micro
 soft/pages/responsepage.aspx?id=NL4TEdGuAE2rS83QJRC-kUTyy7TLuDdAsrmI5CM6E
 KNURDVIOVhQTEk5SE1DTEVEQ0RQNzAwN0lXVC4u&amp\;route=shorturl)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<ul><li><p>      $100 first-place prize in e
 ach category    </p></li><li><p>      Top 3 photos in each category will 
 be displayed in GISB Atrium\, Nov 16 - 20.    </p></li><li><p>      Winni
 ng photos will be permanently displayed in the Global and International S
 tudies Building.    </p></li></ul><p><strong>Who can enter?</strong></p><
 p>  Any HLS student who studied abroad Fall 2025\, Spring 2026\, Summer 2
 026 or Academic Year 2025-2026.</p><p>  Photos must have been taken durin
 g your study abroad experience in your host country.</p><p><strong>Photo 
 Submission Categories</strong></p><ul><li><p><strong>Most Picturesque</st
 rong>: Capture a memorable landscape\, cityscape\, landmark\, or other sc
 ene from your host country    </p></li><li><p><strong>Cultural Exchange:<
 /strong> Share a moment that reflects meaningful engagement with or learn
 ing about your host community and culture    </p></li><li><p><strong>A Da
 y in the Life:&#160\;</strong>Show us a moment that captures what everyda
 y life was like during your time abroad.    </p></li></ul><p><em>Photos t
 hat feature you and your IU spirit are encouraged!</em></p><p><strong>A f
 ew things to know before you submit:</strong></p><p>  Photos should tell 
 the story of your study abroad experience while respectfully representing
  the people and places you encountered</p><ul><li>Make sure people pictur
 ed are comfortable being photographed and having the photo publicly displ
 ayed  </li><li>Photo featuring children or minors are not permitted  </li
 ><li>Do not submit photos featuring dangerous/prohibited activities\, alc
 ohol or drugs.&#160\;  </li><li>Avoid photos that stereotype\, exploit\, 
 or disrespect people or cultures  </li><li>Follow photography rules at re
 ligious\, memorial\, governmental\, and culturally significant sites  </l
 i></ul><p><a href="https://indiana-my.sharepoint.com/:w:/g/personal/ellco
 hen_iu_edu/IQCuZXL_BuC3SJQbjsVO7gvaAbUpX29xqtIFzjJ7JXaPBlY?e=6PUNCr">Revi
 ew the full photo ethics and contest guidelines</a></p><p><strong>Photo S
 pecifications</strong></p><p>  Submit your original\, highest resolution 
 photo (preferably 900 x 720 megapixels or greater)–not a screenshot or 
 imagine downloaded from social media.</p><p>  Low-resolution images may b
 e removed from consideration.</p><p>  Accepted file types: JPEG\, PNG</p>
 <p><a href="https://forms.cloud.microsoft/pages/responsepage.aspx?id=NL4T
 EdGuAE2rS83QJRC-kUTyy7TLuDdAsrmI5CM6EKNURDVIOVhQTEk5SE1DTEVEQ0RQNzAwN0lXV
 C4u&amp\;route=shorturl">Submit your photos here</a></p>
