SUMMARY:How to Build Academic Posters
DESCRIPTION:Join the HLS Graduate Peer Mentors for a practical workshop o
 n how to create an effective academic research poster. We'll discuss how 
 to organize your research\, communicate your main ideas visually\, and de
 sign a poster that works well for conferences\, symposia\, and other acad
 emic settings.  This workshop is the first in a series of events leading 
 up to the Graduate Student Poster Session at the GAP Symposium at HLS on 
 November 7. A follow-up Academic Poster Workshop on October 29 will provi
 de an opportunity to work on your poster and receive feedback before the 
 symposium.  No finished project or previous poster experience is required
 . Whether you already have research you would like to present or simply w
 ant to learn more about academic poster design\, you are welcome to join 
 us.
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  Join the HLS Graduate Peer Mentors for 
 a practical workshop on how to create an effective academic research post
 er. We'll discuss how to organize your research\, communicate your main i
 deas visually\, and design a poster that works well for conferences\, sym
 posia\, and other academic settings.</p><p>  This workshop is the first i
 n a series of events leading up to the Graduate Student Poster Session at
  the GAP Symposium at HLS on November 7. A follow-up Academic Poster Work
 shop on October 29 will provide an opportunity to work on your poster and
  receive feedback before the symposium.</p><p>  No finished project or pr
 evious poster experience is required. Whether you already have research y
 ou would like to present or simply want to learn more about academic post
 er design\, you are welcome to join us.</p>
