LOCATION:GLOBAL &amp\; INTERNATIONAL STUDIES BUILDING
GEO:39.170002;-86.517492
SUMMARY:Global Competencies Skills Development Series: Multilateral Negot
 iations — Preparing to Get Consensus on a United Nations Resolution
DESCRIPTION:What Is This? Can't stay the whole time\, that is ok. This is
  a drop-in session.&#160\;  &#160\;  No boring PowerPoint presentations. 
 No passive lectures.As part of theGlobal Competencies Skills Development 
 Series\, this 2-hour interactive simulation drops you directly into a liv
 e humanitarian crisis scenario whereyoucall the shots. You'll work in int
 erdisciplinary teams to navigate high-stakes international negotiations w
 here conflicting political interests\, limited resources\, and rapid dead
 lines are on the line.  What You'll Get Out of It (Why You Need to Be Her
 e)Day 1 Professional Tradecraft:Learn how diplomats and international cri
 sis managers actually negotiate when peace talks stall or aid lines break
 .  Resume-Boosting Hard Skills:Gain hands-on practice inCritical Thinking
 \, Strategic Communication\, Crisis Leadership\, and Teamwork—the top c
 ompetencies global employers look for.  Direct Access to a Top Senior Exe
 cutive:Work shoulder-to-shoulder with a veteran who managed over$4 Billio
 nin international humanitarian aid and led UN refugee delegations.  Open 
 to ALL staff\, students\, and faculty\, and general public:Whether you're
  in HLS\, O'Neill\, Cybersecurity\, Data Science\, or Public Policy—und
 ergrad or grad—these skills transfer directly to tech\, government\, in
 telligence\, and international NGO careers.    Meet the Expert Paula Reed
  Lynchspent nearly five decades on the front lines of U.S. foreign policy
  and international relief. Serving 14 years in theSenior Executive Servic
 ewithin the Department of State's Bureau of Population\, Refugees\, and M
 igration (PRM)\, Paula oversaw budgets exceeding$4 billionfor global disa
 ster and refugee assistance.      The Highlights:    First American Rappo
 rteur for the UN High Commissioner for Refugees (UNHCR).        Led inter
 agency strategy across the Department of State and USAID.            Help
 ed set global standards for international refugee protection across Afric
 a and worldwide.            Recipient of the Secretary of State'sCareer A
 chievement Award.
