BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:IU Hamilton Lugar School
DTSTART:20261023T180000Z
DTEND:20261023T190000Z
LOCATION:GLOBAL &amp\; INTERNATIONAL STUDIES BUILDING
GEO:39.170002;-86.517492
SUMMARY:Lecture: "Opportunity or Threat? Environmental\, Social\, and Gov
 ernance (ESG) Transformation in Polish Companies" with Monika Foltyn-Zary
 chta
DESCRIPTION:European Union regulations are pushing companies beyond symbo
 lic ESG compliance and reporting towards genuine socially responsible tra
 nsformation. However\, should Polish firms invest more in ESG transformat
 ion? Will consumers reward such investments through their purchasing deci
 sions? And how will financial markets respond to companies making these i
 nvestments? I will explore these questions in my lecture.  Monika Foltyn-
 Zarychta\, Ph.D.\, is an Associate Professor at the University of Economi
 cs in Katowice\, Poland. Her research focuses on climate change\, sustain
 ability\, and the ethical dimensions of investment decision-making\, with
  particular emphasis on intergenerational justice\, long-term discounting
 \, and cost-benefit analysis. She is currently a Visiting Scholar at the 
 Ostrom Workshop at Indiana University.  Cosponsored by the Polish Studies
  Center and the Byrnes Institute (REEI)
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p>  European Union regulations are pushing 
 companies beyond symbolic ESG compliance and reporting towards genuine so
 cially responsible transformation. However\, should Polish firms invest m
 ore in ESG transformation? Will consumers reward such investments through
  their purchasing decisions? And how will financial markets respond to co
 mpanies making these investments? I will explore these questions in my le
 cture.</p><p>  Monika Foltyn-Zarychta\, Ph.D.\, is an Associate Professor
  at the University of Economics in Katowice\, Poland. Her research focuse
 s on climate change\, sustainability\, and the ethical dimensions of inve
 stment decision-making\, with particular emphasis on intergenerational ju
 stice\, long-term discounting\, and cost-benefit analysis. She is current
 ly a Visiting Scholar at the Ostrom Workshop at Indiana University.</p><p
 >  Cosponsored by the Polish Studies Center and the Byrnes Institute (REE
 I)</p>
UID:20261023T180000Z-2402263@events.iu.edu
DTSTAMP:20260831T153747Z
URL:https://events.iu.edu/live/events/2391957-lecture-opportunity-or-thre
