SUMMARY:Global Competencies Skills Development Series: White House Situat
 ion Room to Big Tech - Career Dinner w/ Belinda Jackson Farrier & Shelby 
 Smith-Wilson
DESCRIPTION:Cold messages on LinkedIn rarely lead to meaningful career br
 eakthroughs. This session gives you direct\, unscripted access to two sen
 ior executives whose careers bridge the highest levels of international d
 iplomacy\, national security\, and Silicon Valley leadership.  Feel free 
 to drop in as your schedule allows and stay for as long as your evening p
 ermits. You do not need to attend the full duration to participate\, grab
  dinner\, and engage with our guests.  Who You Will Meet  You will connec
 t directly with two former Senior Foreign Service officers and global exe
 cutive leaders:A Former Director for Global Rapid Response at Google (You
 Tube Trust &amp\; Safety): A career diplomat who served in the White Hous
 e Situation Room and the State Department Operations Center before transi
 tioning to top tier tech leadership.    A Senior Government Executive &am
 p\; Diplomat across 5 Countries: An expert in crisis management\, strateg
 ic negotiations\, and executive leadership who prepares senior officials 
 for high stakes global environments.      Together\, they also co-host th
 e Leadership Tea Podcast and run their own executive advisory firms.  Val
 ue for Every Degree LevelUndergraduate Students: Learn how to break into 
 competitive sectors like foreign policy\, national security\, and tech st
 rategy directly from women who held those roles.    Master Students: Get 
 realistic strategies for translating government and public policy tradecr
 aft into high value roles in corporate policy\, tech\, and consulting.   
  PhD Candidates: Learn how to compress complex academic research into pun
 chy executive briefs that cabinet secretaries and C-suite leaders actuall
 y read.      Key Discussion TopicsWriting Under Pressure: Mastering Botto
 m Line Up Front frameworks for high level decision makers.    The Governm
 ent to Tech Pivot: Moving from government operations to senior roles in S
 ilicon Valley.    Crisis Leadership: Managing teams and making critical d
 ecisions when information is limited and stakes are high.      Speaker Pr
 ofilesBelinda Jackson Farrier  Belinda Jackson Farrier is the Founder of 
 Sweetgrass Advisory Group and co-host of the Leadership Tea Podcast. She 
 served as a career member of the Senior Foreign Service with the U.S. Dep
 artment of State\, holding postings in Rwanda\, El Salvador\, Togo\, and 
 Peru. In Washington\, her assignments included the State Department Opera
 tions Center\, the White House Situation Room\, and the Washington Foreig
 n Press Center. She later joined Google\, where she served as Director fo
 r Global Rapid Response in YouTube Trust and Safety.Shelby Smith-Wilson  
 Shelby Smith-Wilson is the Founder of The FendAll Collaborative and co-ho
 st of the Leadership Tea Podcast. A senior government executive\, diploma
 t\, and leadership strategist\, her global career spans five countries. S
 he specializes in change and crisis management\, strategic negotiation\, 
 and cross-cultural leadership\, advising senior executives on guiding org
 anizations through complex structural transitions and high stakes disrupt
 ions.
